{"dog":{"age_group":"adult","application_url":"https://www.muddypawsrescue.org/adopt","availability_detail":"available","breed_display":"Unknown","breed_primary":"Unknown","description_text":"Maggie is a friendly, outgoing girl who believes the world is full of best friends she hasn't met yet. When she spots a potential new friend, her tail gets going and the rest of her body can't help but wiggle right along with it. She’ll probably even flop down for belly rubs!\n\nShe absolutely adores attention, so naturally she's happiest when she's cuddled up with her people on the couch. She has a gentle, loving nature and truly doesn't seem to have a mean bone in her body.\n\nMaggie also has a bright, curious mind. She's eager to engage with the world around her, and she approaches new challenges with focus rather than frustration. She's the kind of dog who wants to learn, wants to participate, and is always ready for whatever comes next.\n\nMaggie is sweet, loving, and playful, and she's excited to join a patient and loving home!\n\n﻿Maggie is approximately 5y 3m 17d old and is fully grown at 50 pounds. They are microchipped and up to date on all age-appropriate medical care. Their breed is unknown as we have not had a DNA test done.\n\nAlthough our dogs are listed as unknown breed, buildings with specific dog restrictions typically enforce their rules based on what breeds a dog appears to resemble. It's always important to keep that in mind and know your building's policies before adopting a dog.\n\nThis dog is available for adoption through Muddy Paws Rescue. If you're interested in adopting, the first thing you should do is begin the registration process at www.muddypawsrescue.org. If you are already a registered adopter with Muddy Paws Rescue, please email us at adoptionmeetings@muddypawsrescue.org.","detail_url":"https://www.muddypawsrescue.org/adoptable?dog=009939","id":"5975fea967475c569133fec5bd1be29e","image_urls":["https://photos.smugmug.com/Adoption-Events/Regula